# The smallest number of the format not below a 2-limb x: x0, or its successor when x is above
# x0, that is when x1 > 0.
kernel:        to_up_2
input:         x = x0 x1
output:        t
value:         x
requires:      normalized x
ensures:       rounded t up
min_precision: 1
theorem:       proofs/theories/Convert.v to_up_2_correct
source:        the sign of x1 (Milestone 1 listing)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        proved
cone_exempt:   t is x0 or succ(x0), chosen by select, and succ(-inf) is finite; the non-finite layer tests x0 itself

m = lt(0, x1)
s = succ(x0)
t = select(m, s, x0)
